Z||000005||BAM-BAM||07-02-2000||09:19 PM||||  Greg, I'm sure you could. Afterall, it is a Fiero 2.8L V6. Should be a direct bolt and go. <P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000006||HYPTNOTiSE||07-03-2000||10:57 AM||||Not necessarily greg.  Some 2.8's are externally balanced, and they have different flywheel/flexplate combinations than the internally balanced engines. Internally balanced engines are superior to externally balanced because they are nicer to the bearings and such.  In fieros 85-87 were externally balanced, and if you have a manual you'll notice a large bump on the backside of the flywheel, this is how the engine is balanced. Internally balanced flywheels use nothing, they're flywheels are neutrally balanced.  So if you've already had a v6 replacement,and you're car's an 85 i'd venture to say that you're engine is still externally balanced. But you never know. If you'd want to change over you'd have to buy an 88 flywheel, a DOHC 3.4 flywheel, or a flywheel from joe wynman. They're about another 200 bucks.<P><P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||07-03-2000||12:28 PM||||OK so if I understand corerectly, I COULD use the motor, with the 85 4speed Muncie, but I would need to get one of the above mentioned  flywheels.  <P>What about the computer and wiring harness that I guess would be the same as long as I was using the accessories that came with my 85.<P>Oh this engine sounds like it would make me a happy camper!<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||07-03-2000||12:45 PM||||  Greg, other than the flywheeel, you would just use al the other neccessary components ie...sensors, fuel rail, lower intake, plenum and so on. what ever this engine doesn't have, use off your donor engine or go to Nevada Pic-A-Part in Henderson. they have several Fiero's. Or their sister location at Lamm and Graig. Either way this would be an awesome addition to your Fiero. If you do not have a V6 already you will need the harness and ECM also.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||10
